Last week Jon attended the Tokyo Game Show as part of a new Creative Wales trade mission! Wales had a strong presence in the Indie hall and Planted! was front and centre on both the Cloth Cat Games stand and the @curveball_games stand! Loads of attendees played the game, adding it to their wishlists and demanding the Switch version! Jon got to explore the huge halls over the three main days and got a better understanding of the Japanese market. He looks forward to returning again next year!

A massive thank you to Kathryn Wolfe-Adams, Beth Romais and Carl Plested for organising and supporting the trade mission. Also a big shout out to all the other companies and exciting games on the Wales stand. We're on the cusp of a new games revolution in Wales!

